# The tiles are the artefact; the PNGs beside them are not.
#
# tools/demo_photos.py writes only the .bin files by default. Its --keep-src
# flag leaves the 8-bit source next to each one and --preview leaves what the
# screened tile actually looks like on the panel, and both exist because a
# pipeline whose output cannot be looked at is a pipeline nobody checks. They
# are how the plates were judged; they are not deliverables, they are derived
# from committed inputs by a deterministic script, and they are about 700 KB.
#
# Committing derived images beside the artefacts they were derived from is hard
# to undo later, so they are ignored here rather than left to a habit of
# remembering to delete them.
*.png
